   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Using the same data as in Problem 1, assume that ABC Company expects a 10% increase in sales in the coming year (10% more than the $575,000 it had in the past year). Prepare its sales forecast, assuming the company breaks its sales down by month using the same percentages as the actual sales from the past year, which you calculated in the first problem.\n<img src=\"exercises/media/0cd27691d978031f.png\" alt=\"Monthly income statement of ABC company shows empty cells for gross sales on a monthly basis and the percentage of annual sales.\">",
